      "writtenOn": "2021-08-05T01:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After taking a look, it turns out that way that typeface_styling is requesting hairlines they are not actually being drawn by the SkScalerContext here, see SkGlyphRunListPainter::drawForBitmapDevice where SkStrikeSpec::ShouldDrawAsPath returns true because hairline glyphs are just drawn as paths. (The SkScalerContext handles hairlines for code paths other than this.) SkStrikeSpec::MakePath always gets a \"Fill\" style path with no path effect and then applies these properties when drawing instead.\n\nWhich explains why when I was tweaking the SkScalerContext drawing bits this particular test in this configuration wasn\u0027t changing.",
      "revId": "0dc4555158b090f765161d677a6b0d97396e38e8",
